##
## modelstack overlay — THIS PROJECT IS PUBLIC (operator decision, 2026-09-14; layout migrated 2026-09-15)
##
# Everything the framework supplies now lives under ONE directory, `vendor/` — the pinned runtime
# unit (`vendor/{contracts,decision,prompts,relay,runtime,stack,telemetry}`) and the stamped
# maintenance overlay (`vendor/AGENTS.md`, `vendor/conductor/`, `vendor/docs/`,
# `vendor/.reasonix/skills/`, `vendor/config.yaml` + the engine yamls, `vendor/housekeeping_guard.py`,
# `vendor/hooks/pre-commit`, the `*.fragment` set, `vendor/stack_adapter.py`,
# `vendor/PROJECTS.fragment.json`, `vendor/ISSUE_template.md`). None of it is the extension, and none
# of it belongs in the extension's history.
#
# What excludes it is the GENERATED region at the bottom of this file — three patterns written by
# `msf public --enable` (`/vendor/`, `/modelstack.lock`, `/reasonix.toml*`) — not a hand-written list,
# so a file the framework stamps tomorrow cannot leak: it arrives under `vendor/`. The 40 hand-written
# patterns this block replaces were reconciled one by one in
# `temp/archived/ISSUE_vendored_overlay_layout_and_generated_public_block_20260915.md` §4 + §6.3:
# 14 became unnecessary and 3 are now supplied by the region below, so 23 patterns STAY — this
# project's own rules, which the generated region makes no claim on (the 9 reviewer/consultation
# artifact SHAPES, the 6 project-authored harness gates, working state, the agent binary,
# `/.gitattributes`, `/AGENTS.md`). Do not delete them to "get to three lines". The kept set is 25 as
# of the governance adoption of 2026-09-15: the 23 patterns that reconciliation kept, plus the
# `/test/unit/vendored_overlay.test.js` layout pin the migration itself added, plus
# `/governance.yaml` — needed because the gate reads that declaration at the ROOT only
# (`framework/runtime/governance.py:96`) and `/vendor/` cannot reach it.
#
# Consequence, unchanged from 2026-09-14: `AGENTS.md`'s older rule — "commit `vendor/` beside
# `modelstack.lock`" — does not hold here. The pin is provenance in the worktree; a rollback
# re-materialises the unit with `modelstack sync --target . --from <unit_revision>`.
# `core.hooksPath` is repository-local, so a fresh clone carries the block and NOT the hook: re-run
# `msf public --enable` there to re-bind it (framework residual R2).

# Project working state — scratch, telemetry, run logs, the issue handoffs the housekeeping guard
# reads. None of it is product, and the load-bearing parts are regenerated by the guard, not
# restored from git.
/temp/

# Browser-gate and probe screenshots (generated by scripts/screenshot.js and the collage probes):
# run artifacts, not evidence — the measurements they fed live in vendor/docs/.
/shots/

# Reasonix's own run state. The directory stays at the root because its path is hardcoded in the
# client (`reasonix-upstream/internal/cli/task.go:72` -> `.reasonix/tasks`); the playbooks it used to
# hold are under `vendor/.reasonix/skills/` now, declared to the client by `[skills] paths` in
# `reasonix.toml`.
/.reasonix/

# The root AGENTS.md POINTER: a shim that @imports `vendor/AGENTS.md`, needed because Reasonix has no
# config key for extra instruction-document paths (`internal/instruction/resolver.go:24` hardcodes the
# names and walks the workspace chain). It is framework prose, so it is excluded exactly as
# `vendor/AGENTS.md` is — a public clone carries neither.
/AGENTS.md

# The governance declaration: framework-stamped, but it MUST sit at the root because the gate reads
# it at `root / "governance.yaml"` (`modelstack_framework/framework/runtime/governance.py:96`) — that
# one lookup does not go through the `vendor_layout.resolve_home` seam the unit homes use, so a copy
# under `vendor/` is never read. A FIFTH root-resident framework artifact beside the census' three and
# the `AGENTS.md` pointer above; `/vendor/` cannot reach it, so it is named here. The fleet's other
# vendored consumers place it at the root for the same reason (MEASURED 2026-09-15).
/governance.yaml

# The operator-provided agent binary, not project source.
/reasonix
/reasonix.exe
/reasonix.exe.prev-*

# THIS project's own line-ending policy file (authored here 2026-09-11 — `modelstack init` does not
# stamp one, so `/vendor/` cannot cover it). It must stay at the worktree root to be honoured; its
# rules keep a checkout of vendor/** and modelstack.lock byte-identical.
/.gitattributes

# Project-authored harness helpers that police the gates above (framework residual R3: "project-authored
# harness helpers stay where the project put them" — the generated region makes no claim on them).
/scripts/input_budget_report.py
/scripts/verify_lanes.py
/scripts/muse_gate.py
/scripts/utility_telemetry.py
/test/unit/utility_telemetry.test.js
/test/unit/housekeeping_guard.test.js
/test/unit/lanes_aliases.test.js
/test/unit/input_budget_alignment.test.js
/test/unit/vendored_overlay.test.js

##
## Reviewer / consultation artifacts — NOT PART OF THE PRODUCT (operator decision, 2026-09-14)
##
# Muse and the visual-gate reviewers produce a file per round: the brief sent, the raw reply, and a
# verdict. That is the *process*, not the product — a reader needs the measurement a round produced,
# which lives in the track's `final_report.md`, the README and the committed frames.
#
# Patterns are the artifact SHAPES, not a directory, so a future track cannot re-add them by naming its
# evidence directory something slightly different. Most now sit under `vendor/{conductor,docs}/` and so
# are already covered by `/vendor/`; they are KEPT because their stated purpose is about shape, and
# they still guard the same artifact names under any path this project DOES track.
**/reviews-phase*/
**/reviews/
**/consult/
**/consult-*.md
**/consult_*.md
**/consult_log.md
**/muse_review*.md
**/vision_review*.md
**/*_execution_review*.md
# >>> modelstack vendor overlay (generated — do not edit) >>>
# <why: this project is declared public; everything the framework supplies lives in vendor/>
/vendor/
/modelstack.lock
/reasonix.toml*
# <<< modelstack vendor overlay (generated) <<<
